cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CPUQuotaLab, please cite this preliminary software and research artifact."
type: software
title: "CPUQuotaLab: Beyond Core Counts"
authors:
  - family-names: "Singh"
    given-names: "Mohit"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Rust and Linux cgroup-v2 experimental artifact for studying how fractional
  CPU quotas, bandwidth periods, and native worker-pool sizing affect
  end-to-end latency, throughput, request outcomes, and CPU accounting under
  mixed-duration CPU-bound workloads. Results are preliminary, single-machine,
  independent undergraduate research and are not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - Linux
  - cgroup v2
  - CPU quotas
  - thread pools
  - tail latency
  - systems research
